# The loopback tunnel's key material, generated per machine by the launcher.
#
# PRIVATE KEYS. Committing tunnel-key or tunnel-host-key would publish one keypair to every
# student and every reader of the repository, which is exactly the reason they are generated
# per machine instead of baked into the image. The public halves and known_hosts are matched
# too: they are per-machine derived files with nothing to gain from being tracked, and a
# stale committed copy would be worse than none.
#
# The pattern covers tunnel-key, tunnel-key.pub, tunnel-host-key, tunnel-host-key.pub and
# tunnel-known-hosts in one line, so a future addition beside them is ignored by default
# rather than by remembering to come back here.
.config/tunnel-*

# Student work. The directory itself is tracked (via .gitkeep) so the bind mount target
# always exists; nothing inside it is.
projects/*
!projects/.gitkeep

.DS_Store

# Python bytecode. files/shortlink is a python3 program, so anyone who reaches for
# `python3 -m py_compile` on it -- the obvious way to syntax-check one -- drops a
# __pycache__ beside it. Both the Containerfile and 10-static.sh use `compile()` instead,
# for exactly that reason; this is here for the times somebody does it by hand anyway.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
